"""A dedicated HEX-plus-opacity workflow; the existing RGB converter keeps its semantics."""
RGBA_TOOL=('hex-to-rgba','HEX to RGBA','CSS & layout','Add opacity to a HEX color, preview transparency and copy RGBA or 8-digit HEX.','palette')

def rgba_page(tool_head,copy,docs,extra_section,ad_slot,related):
 body=tool_head('hex-to-rgba','CSS & COLOR','HEX to RGBA converter','Turn a HEX color into RGBA with an explicit opacity. Preview the color over light and dark backgrounds, copy CSS, and compare its nearest 8-digit HEX value.')
 body+='''<section class="workbench rgba-workbench"><div class="bench-toolbar"><strong>HEX color + opacity</strong><span class="quiet">sRGB channels · runs locally</span></div><div class="bench-body"><div class="input-panel"><label for="rgba-input">HEX color</label><input id="rgba-input" class="mono" value="#244cda" spellcheck="false" autocomplete="off"><p class="hint">3, 4, 6 or 8 digits, with or without #. In CSS, alpha comes last.</p><label for="rgba-alpha">Opacity for 3- or 6-digit HEX</label><input id="rgba-alpha" type="number" min="0" max="1" step="any" value="0.5"><p class="hint" id="rgba-alpha-note">Use 0 for transparent and 1 for opaque. A 4- or 8-digit value supplies its own alpha.</p><div class="actions"><button class="button ghost" id="rgba-clear">Clear</button></div><p class="mono-label example-label">TRY A COMPLETE EXAMPLE</p><div class="example-buttons"><button class="button small" data-rgba-example="#244cda" data-opacity="0.5">50% opacity</button><button class="button small" data-rgba-example="#33669980">8-digit HEX</button><button class="button small" data-rgba-example="#0f08">Short alpha</button><button class="button small" data-rgba-example="#00000000">Transparent</button></div><p class="error" id="rgba-error" role="alert" hidden></p></div><div class="result-panel"><div class="rgba-preview"><div id="rgba-fill"></div><span>Light background</span><span>Dark background</span></div><div class="result-head"><label class="mono-label" for="rgba-output">RGBA RESULT</label>'''+copy('rgba-output')+'''</div><input id="rgba-output" class="mono" value="rgba(36, 76, 218, 0.5)" readonly><div class="result-head"><label class="mono-label" for="rgba-hex-output">NEAREST 8-DIGIT HEX</label>'''+copy('rgba-hex-output')+'''</div><input id="rgba-hex-output" class="mono" value="#244CDA80" readonly><p class="result-sub" id="rgba-note" role="status">RGBA opacity 0.5 maps to alpha byte 128/255 in HEX.</p><div class="result-head"><span class="mono-label">CSS EXAMPLE</span>'''+copy('rgba-css','Copy CSS')+'''</div><pre class="rgba-css"><code id="rgba-css">.overlay {
  background-color: rgba(36, 76, 218, 0.5);
}</code></pre></div></div></section>'''
 body+=ad_slot('tool_primary')+docs('How to convert HEX to RGBA','Enter a color, then set an opacity from 0 to 1. A 6-digit color gives the red, green and blue bytes; opacity supplies the fourth RGBA component. An 8-digit color already contains alpha, so the separate opacity control is disabled.','#RRGGBB + opacity → rgba(R, G, B, opacity)',[
 ('Where is alpha in an 8-digit CSS HEX color?','CSS uses #RRGGBBAA: the last two digits are alpha. #33669980 contains red 51, green 102, blue 153 and alpha 128/255, approximately 0.501961. Formats that put alpha first are different; rearrange them before using this converter.'),
 ('Does #80 mean exactly 50% opacity?','No. Hexadecimal 80 is decimal 128. Dividing by 255 gives approximately 0.501961. An RGBA opacity of 0.5 is exact as written; its nearest 8-bit HEX alpha is 80. This page preserves a separately entered RGBA opacity and explains the small HEX rounding difference.'),
 ('What does a 4-digit color mean?','Each digit is doubled: #0f08 becomes #00ff0088. Its green channel is 255 and its opacity is 136/255, about 0.533333. This is shorthand for four channels, not a shortened six-digit color.'),
 ('Why is the preview different over white and dark backgrounds?','A partially transparent color is composited with whatever is behind it. The converter shows the same foreground over two backgrounds; it does not change the RGB channels or bake the background into the output.'),
 ('Is alpha the same as the CSS opacity property?','Alpha affects the color value where you use it, such as background-color. Setting opacity on an element also affects the rendered element and its contents, including text and children. Use a color alpha when only that painted color should be translucent.'),
 ('Can I paste an rgba() function or convert back?','This entry point accepts HEX and a separate decimal opacity. For separate RGB/RGBA channel input and reverse conversion, use the HEX to RGB tool. Named colors, HSL and wide-gamut color spaces are outside this page’s input format.'),
 ],'<a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Values/hex-color">MDN: HEX color syntax</a> · <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/opacity">MDN: element opacity</a>')
 body+=extra_section('hex-alpha','8-digit HEX and opacity, step by step','Use the same color in both notations, while keeping the alpha rounding visible.','''<div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Step</th><th>Value</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Split #336699</td><td>33 · 66 · 99</td><td>One pair per color channel</td></tr><tr><td>Read decimal channels</td><td>51 · 102 · 153</td><td>Each byte ranges from 0 to 255</td></tr><tr><td>Choose opacity</td><td>0.5</td><td>RGBA keeps the chosen value</td></tr><tr><td>Find the closest alpha byte</td><td>round(0.5 × 255) = 128 = 80</td><td>8-bit HEX must choose a whole byte</td></tr><tr><td>Compare outputs</td><td>rgba(51, 102, 153, 0.5)<br>#33669980</td><td>Nearly, but not exactly, the same alpha</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Use <a href="/hex-to-rgb/">HEX to RGB</a> when you want decimal color channels without adding opacity, or when you need reverse RGB input. That converter keeps its RGBA display aligned with the rounded HEX byte; this entry point keeps a separately entered opacity in the primary RGBA result. Both show their assumptions.</p><p>For a translucent background, apply <code>background-color: rgba(51, 102, 153, 0.5)</code> to the element. Applying <code>opacity: 0.5</code> instead also fades its text and children. Neither this preview nor a valid color code establishes accessible contrast; test the actual foreground, background and text together.</p>''')
 body+=ad_slot('tool_secondary')+related('hex-to-rgba')+'<noscript><p class="hint">JavaScript enables live conversion and copying. The complete default example and reference table remain readable.</p></noscript>'
 return ('hex-to-rgba','HEX to RGBA Converter — Color & Opacity','Convert HEX to RGBA with explicit opacity. Preview transparency, decode 4- or 8-digit alpha, copy CSS and compare the nearest HEX value locally.',body)
